A||||15||ChadMan||The Fiero that got away||||9||
Z||000000||ChadMan||01-10-2001||04:34 PM||||We've talked about Fieros we've owned and loved, and Fieros we've sold and missed.  But how about the Fiero that got away - one you should have bought, but missed your chance?  Let's hear some sob stories...<P>When I was working my internship in college, a coworker had a black 85 SE V6 4-sp that she had bought new.  It had a lot of miles and bad paint, but was straight and never wrecked.  I asked her if she wanted to sell it and she said "no way."  <P>Well, one day I overheard her complaining that her clutch was shot and she'd have to get rid of the Fiero.  I started asking around for someone to bum money off of, but was too late - she came to work in a brand-new (1993) Firebird.  I asked what she did with the Fiero and she said she traded it in - FOR $250!!!  I snoozed - and lost.||||reg||9
Z||000001||Philphine||01-10-2001||04:38 PM||||bake in late fall i could have got an '86 gt with 2 engines (the one installed was bad) for $650. coulda got if i scraped up some cash but decided to wait. sold later that day.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Raydar||01-10-2001||04:41 PM||||In the GA Auto Trader, about 10 months ago, there was an 86 4-speed GT, medium red, with a bad engine. Supposedly was in excellent condition, otherwise. Guy wanted $400-500 for it. It was only about 1/2 hour from the house. Still kicking myself over that one. <BR>The good side of it is, I believe another Forum member got it. ||||reg||9
Z||000003||88formula||01-10-2001||05:53 PM||||I could have bought an 87 GT from Kick Hill Farm with 40,000 miles on it for $3000. I wish I had bought it. <P>||||reg||1
Z||000004||kslish||01-10-2001||06:43 PM||||Well, there was that perfect yellow '88 Formula about two years ago that I missed buying by about two hours.  I was going to meet the seller after I got off of work one day but some guy bought it out from under me by going to where the seller worked with cash in hand and bought it on the spot.  The seller and I only had a verbal agreement at the time so I couldn't do anything about it but cry in my beer.  <P>I should have taken a sick day.....  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Ken S.<BR>'86 SC and '87 GT||||reg||9
Z||000005||sluppy123||01-10-2001||08:15 PM||||About a Year ago I ran across a add in the local paper, 87 GT, Blue, 5-speed, all options. I went and had a look at it, 75k miles perfect inside and out and the lady was asking only $2200 but I had just graduated from college, no job, had three fieros already so I had to let her go.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P><P>------------------<BR>-Brian, Toolmaker<BR>Lincoln, NE<BR>85' SC & 87' GT-Leather, Lowered and On The Bottle<BR> <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=247832&a=1843773&p=29628235&Sequence=0"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||qwikgta||01-10-2001||08:28 PM||||This summer while visiting my Sister her neighbor had an 85 GT, 4spd, loaded with low mileage for sale.  The lady wanted to buy a new camaro and was going to get soaked on a trade.  She was selling it for $1500.  About 2 weeks later she took the best offer...... $700.  I missed it, I had the $700 at the time but i never thought she'd go so low, I never even offered.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>QWIKGTA<BR>88 T-Top<BR>http://robsfieroproject.homestead.com/index.html||||reg||1
Z||000007||Black88GT||01-10-2001||08:48 PM||||kslish, was this in your area?  I know of a similar story around me in Baltimore, just wondering if it might be related....<P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD||||reg||1
Z||000008||FieroMaster88||01-11-2001||01:32 AM||||Last summer, there was a black 86 Gt, i think 5 speed if I remember right, Mint condition, 45,000 miles, tan interior, all options.  The guy was asking $5500 for it.  Didn't have that much.  I would have been able to pay $4000, but didnt offer. Sold for $4000!  DOH!!!!  <P>But then again, I just got my 88 coupe with 30K miles for $4000, so it kinda worked out in the end!  I love the coupe, but the GT.....always wanted one!  Maybe I will get another chance like that again!<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FieroMaster88.gif">  <BR>James Essar<BR>AOL IM Name: FieroMaster86<BR>88 Coupe 30,000 miles<BR>84 Indy Fiero (restoration Project)||||reg||1
Z||000009||fierogt88||01-11-2001||10:38 AM||||3 months ago I stopped at a used car lot that had a red 84.  Took it for a test drive and heard the engine knocking hard.  Everything else was perfect and it had gold gt wheels.  I asked the guy what he was asking and he said to make an offer.  I went home to talk to the wife about what we could scrape up.  When I returned the next day, willing to pay $600 I was grieved to discover that the car had just sold for $75.  I had $100 in my pocket when I test drove it but never even dreamed that a dealer would let a car go for that....||||reg||1
Z||000010||Racer 1||01-11-2001||11:21 AM||||About a year or so ago this guy was selling a gold 1988 GT with sunroof mint condition for $2500. I didnt have the cash but was almost temptedto sell my 86 coupe and get this one. But I could'nt look my fiero in the fascia and tell her she was going for a newer molder. That would have been a jerry springer show. So I had to pass but I dont regret it now. <P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://spitfire.cwv.net/~cdbailey/images/gifssucl/eyes2/evil_eyes.gif"> ||||reg||10
Z||000011||2xsess||01-11-2001||05:02 PM||||Well, I found an Indy online for $990. But, it was in CA, I thought about getting in touch with some of the members here to see if anyone could help out getting it atleast a little closer to me. But I instead posted it here.<P>I should let AL finish this story for me since he bought it for $250  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/005132.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/005132.html</A> <BR><P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>AOL IM : Only2xsess<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/My_car_(large)sig_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000012||Fformula88||01-11-2001||05:25 PM||||I looked at an 86 coupe about a year and a half ago on the local Pontiac dealer's lot.  It had 19,000 original miles on it and was absolutely cherry!  There wasn't a scaratch in the paint or blemish on the interior.  Unfortunately I was still in college, and already had two cars (my Formula and Probe).  There was simply no more money for another Fiero.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">  Its a shame because they were only asking $3500 for it, but I am sure they would have taken a lot less.  It took them about 6 months to sell it.<P>------------------<BR>John<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/formula2m6/FIEROSIG1.JPG">     <BR>1988 Fiero Formula<BR>1997 Ford Probe SE<BR>AOL IM: Fformula88<p>[This message has been edited by Fformula88 (edited 01-11-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000013||Ronnie||01-12-2001||09:06 PM||||Last Spring,I had been seeing a gold fastback GT sitting at a local motorcycle shop.It sat at least 2-3 months.I kept saying I was going to check on it , but before I ever did, IT WAS GONE!!!Snooze, you lose!!!||||reg||6
Z||000014||Cooter||01-12-2001||09:49 PM||||I bought an 88 GT/topper for about $1700, but got into such financial trouble that I could not keep it. I wished it had got away so I would not have to kick myself every time I see it and know that it was mine  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000015||Raydar||01-12-2001||11:29 PM||||Another Auto Trader find...<BR>In September, there was a yellow 5 speed Formula in north GA. Seems like it had 28000 miles. Guy was asking $2300. Had been mildly bumped in the front. Said it needed cleaning up, and paint on the hood and fascia. <BR>Although it sounded neglected, I wish I would have gone and looked. By the time I called him back, it was gone.||||reg||1
